// anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa
// raw#9 hexa-only · raw#10 honest-C3 · raw#11 snake_case · raw#12 frozen
// raw#15 no-personal-paths · raw#34 no-backup-files · raw#65 idempotent
// raw#71 falsifier-bound · raw#80 sentinel · raw#82 darwin-native marker
// raw#91 honest-class · own 5
//
// @resolver-bypass(reason="darwin-native: --run delegates to anima-eeg/collect.hexa
//                   subprocess (BrainFlow + USB-serial dongle on host) and chains
//                   sample_rate_guard.hexa + package_num_audit.hexa for the
//                   --auto-quality-audit step. selftest is pure-hexa synthetic
//                   block design + trend ledger emission; unified bypass keeps
//                   route stable across Darwin / Linux hosts.")
//
// PURPOSE  (raw#106 genus name: long_duration_resting)
//   Long-duration resting-state baseline capture (5 / 10 / 30 minutes) with
//   AI-side quality monitoring and a circadian / drowsiness trend ledger.
//   Unlike alpha_eyes_closed.hexa (block-design EC/EO × 5 min) this protocol
//   is *naturalistic*: cap on, eyes open, daily-life motion permitted, single
//   long capture (or N × segment-minutes split). The capture is indexed by
//   per-segment band-power evolution so the AI can spot drowsiness onset,
//   focus episodes, and circadian α/θ/β shift across the session.
//
//   This file ships:
//     1. Naturalistic block design (single long or multi-segment split)
//     2. Synthetic per-segment band-power trend (selftest)
//     3. Quality-monitoring ledger (paradigm=long_resting, JSONL append)
//     4. Trend metrics sidecar (α/θ/β/δ × segment + EOG blink rate +
//        relaxation index + drowsiness signature θ/α ratio)
//     5. Three frozen falsifiers (F_LR_01/02/03)
//     6. Quality-audit chain hint (sample_rate_guard + package_num_audit)
//
//   Single-author N=1 (raw#10 honest-class C3): daily-life motion artifact
//   is unavoidable, gel impedance drifts over 30 minutes, and circadian state
//   varies by session — see the three caveats at end of file.
//
// LIVE BRAINFLOW INGEST: --run prints a delegated collect.hexa command +
//   audio-cue schedule; raw#10 honest — this protocol does NOT do BrainFlow
//   ingest itself, the actual capture happens via collect.hexa subprocess
//   in a separate terminal (same pattern as alpha_eyes_closed.hexa).
//
// API
//   hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --selftest
//
//   hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --run \
//        --port <serial> --board cyton_daisy --duration <minutes> \
//        [--segment-minutes <n>] [--auto-quality-audit] [--ledger] \
//        [--output <npy>]
//
// FALSIFIERS  (raw#71 frozen 2026-05-03)
//   F_LR_01: total_duration_minutes_actual >= 0.95 × duration_requested_min
//            (95% capture compliance — drift / pause / abort gate)
//   F_LR_02: effective_fs_hz >= 30.0
//            (α-band Nyquist > 13 Hz; matches sample_rate_guard eeg_alpha)
//   F_LR_03: per-segment alpha-band power > 0.0 for every segment
//            (no flat / disconnected channel for any segment)
//
// SENTINEL  (raw#80)
//   __EEG_LONG_RESTING__ <PASS|FAIL> <duration_min> <segments>
//
// HONEST C3 CAVEATS  (raw#10) — see end of file for full text
//   1. Daily-life motion artifact (walking / eating / bathroom)
//   2. Gel impedance drift over 30 minutes (cap dries out)
//   3. Circadian-state baseline variability (morning vs evening vs post-meal)
//
// USAGE
//   # 5-minute baseline, single segment
//   hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --run \
//        --port /dev/cu.usbserial-DP04WGIQ --board cyton_daisy --duration 5
//
//   # 30-minute capture split into 6 × 5-minute segments + auto-audit + ledger
//   hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --run \
//        --port /dev/cu.usbserial-DP04WGIQ --board cyton_daisy \
//        --duration 30 --segment-minutes 5 --auto-quality-audit --ledger

let SCHEMA = "anima-eeg/long_duration_resting/1"

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Frozen capture parameters (raw#12 pre-registered)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

let DEFAULT_DURATION_MIN     = 5            // baseline default
let DEFAULT_SEGMENT_MIN      = 5            // split granularity default
let MIN_DURATION_MIN         = 5            // floor (paradigm contract)
let MAX_DURATION_MIN         = 30           // ceiling (gel-drift cap)
let CUE_INTERVAL_MIN         = 5            // "측정 중" announce every N min
let SEGMENT_PAUSE_S          = 0            // default no inter-segment pause

// Board / signal-chain frozen (matches alpha_eyes_closed.hexa)
let SAMPLE_RATE_HZ           = 250          // Cyton+Daisy native
let CHANNEL_COUNT            = 16
let NOTCH_HZ                 = 60.0
let BANDPASS_LO_HZ           = 1.0
let BANDPASS_HI_HZ           = 50.0

// Frequency band edges (Hz) — frozen
let DELTA_LO_HZ              = 1.0
let DELTA_HI_HZ              = 4.0
let THETA_LO_HZ              = 4.0
let THETA_HI_HZ              = 8.0
let ALPHA_LO_HZ              = 8.0          // standard α (Berger 1929 wider)
let ALPHA_HI_HZ              = 13.0
let BETA_LO_HZ               = 13.0
let BETA_HI_HZ               = 30.0

// Falsifier thresholds
let F_LR_01_DURATION_FRAC    = 0.95         // ≥ 95% of requested
let F_LR_02_FS_FLOOR_HZ      = 30.0         // α-band Nyquist
let F_LR_03_ALPHA_FLOOR      = 0.0          // strict > 0

// Trend signature thresholds (for sidecar annotation, not falsifiers)
let DROWSY_THETA_ALPHA_RATIO = 1.20         // θ/α > this = drowsy candidate
let RELAX_O_ALPHA_FLOOR_UV2  = 8.0          // O1/O2 α > this = relaxed

// Audit / ledger paths
let AUDIT_DIR  = "state/long_duration_resting_audit"
let LEDGER_DIR = "state/quality_monitoring_ledger"

// Channel mapping (10-20; user must verify physical placement)
let CHAN_FP1                 = "Fp1"        // EOG (blink rate)
let CHAN_FP2                 = "Fp2"        // EOG (blink rate)
let CHAN_O1                  = "O1"         // α relaxation index
let CHAN_O2                  = "O2"         // α relaxation index

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Globals (raw#9 strict — no fallbacks, all measured)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// Schedule
let g_duration_min           = 0
let g_segment_min            = 0
let g_segment_count          = 0
let g_total_seconds          = 0

// Per-segment trend (synthetic in selftest, populated post-capture in --run)
let g_seg0_alpha_uv2         = 0.0
let g_seg0_theta_uv2         = 0.0
let g_seg0_beta_uv2          = 0.0
let g_seg0_delta_uv2         = 0.0
let g_seg_last_alpha_uv2     = 0.0
let g_seg_last_theta_uv2     = 0.0
let g_seg_last_beta_uv2      = 0.0
let g_seg_last_delta_uv2     = 0.0
let g_min_alpha_uv2          = 0.0          // for F_LR_03 evaluation
let g_blink_rate_per_min     = 0.0          // Fp1/Fp2 EOG
let g_relax_index_o          = 0.0          // (O1+O2)/2 alpha
let g_drowsy_signature       = 0.0          // last-seg θ/α ratio

// Capture quality (post-capture sample_rate_guard echo)
let g_effective_fs_hz        = 0.0
let g_actual_duration_min    = 0.0
let g_duration_fraction      = 0.0

// Falsifier evaluations (raw#71)
let g_f_lr_01_pass           = false        // duration >= 95% of requested
let g_f_lr_02_pass           = false        // effective_fs >= 30 Hz
let g_f_lr_03_pass           = false        // per-segment α > 0

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Helpers
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn abs_f(x: float) -> float {
    if x < 0.0 { return 0.0 - x }
    return x
}

fn _bool_str(b: bool) -> string {
    if b { return "true" }
    return "false"
}

fn min_f(a: float, b: float) -> float {
    if a < b { return a }
    return b
}

fn safe_div(a: float, b: float) -> float {
    let mut bb = b
    if abs_f(bb) < 0.000001 {
        if bb < 0.0 { bb = 0.0 - 0.000001 } else { bb = 0.000001 }
    }
    return a / bb
}

fn _ensure_dir(path: string) {
    let _rc = exec("mkdir -p " + path)
}

// Clamp duration into [MIN, MAX]
fn _clamp_duration(d: int) -> int {
    let mut v = d
    if v < MIN_DURATION_MIN { v = MIN_DURATION_MIN }
    if v > MAX_DURATION_MIN { v = MAX_DURATION_MIN }
    return v
}

// Clamp segment-minutes into [1, duration]
fn _clamp_segment(seg: int, dur: int) -> int {
    let mut v = seg
    if v < 1   { v = 1 }
    if v > dur { v = dur }
    return v
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Block schedule generator (raw#65 idempotent — no RNG needed)
//   single long capture or N × segment-minutes
//   audio cues at every CUE_INTERVAL_MIN ("측정 중")
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn build_schedule(duration_min: int, segment_min: int) {
    g_duration_min   = _clamp_duration(duration_min)
    g_segment_min    = _clamp_segment(segment_min, g_duration_min)
    // ceil(duration / segment) — integer math (duration is multiple in nominal use)
    let mut n = g_duration_min / g_segment_min
    if (n * g_segment_min) < g_duration_min { n = n + 1 }
    g_segment_count  = n
    g_total_seconds  = g_duration_min * 60
}

// Returns audio cue text for time t (seconds since session start).
fn cue_text_at_t(t_sec: int) -> string {
    if t_sec == 0 { return "측정 시작 (begin)" }
    let mins = t_sec / 60
    return "측정 중 t=" + to_string(mins) + "분 (continue)"
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Synthetic per-segment trend (selftest pathway)
//   Pure-math evolution (no RNG). Models a typical 30-minute resting
//   session with mild drowsiness onset:
//     seg0:  alert baseline    α=12, θ=6,  β=8, δ=4  (relaxed eyes-open)
//     drift: α grows slightly, θ grows faster (drowsy onset),
//            β stable, δ stable
//     last:  α=14, θ=10, β=8, δ=4   (θ/α ratio ~0.71 — borderline)
//   Caller specifies "perturb_*" flags to exercise falsifiers in tests.
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

let SYNTH_SEG0_ALPHA_UV2     = 12.0
let SYNTH_SEG0_THETA_UV2     =  6.0
let SYNTH_SEG0_BETA_UV2      =  8.0
let SYNTH_SEG0_DELTA_UV2     =  4.0
let SYNTH_DRIFT_ALPHA_PER    =  0.3          // grow per segment
let SYNTH_DRIFT_THETA_PER    =  0.7
let SYNTH_BLINK_RATE_NOMINAL = 18.0          // per minute (relaxed adult)
let SYNTH_FS_NOMINAL_HZ      = 248.0         // ~99% of native 250 Hz
let SYNTH_DUR_FRAC_NOMINAL   = 0.99

fn analyze_synthetic_trend(
    perturb_short_capture: bool,
    perturb_low_fs: bool,
    perturb_flat_alpha: bool
) {
    // Duration fraction default
    let mut dur_frac = SYNTH_DUR_FRAC_NOMINAL
    if perturb_short_capture { dur_frac = 0.80 }   // user removed cap early
    g_duration_fraction   = dur_frac
    g_actual_duration_min = dur_frac * g_duration_min

    // Effective fs default
    let mut fs = SYNTH_FS_NOMINAL_HZ
    if perturb_low_fs { fs = 22.0 }                // simulate Daisy collapse
    g_effective_fs_hz = fs

    // Per-segment band evolution
    let n  = g_segment_count
    let nf = n
    let last_idx = nf - 1

    // First segment
    g_seg0_alpha_uv2 = SYNTH_SEG0_ALPHA_UV2
    g_seg0_theta_uv2 = SYNTH_SEG0_THETA_UV2
    g_seg0_beta_uv2  = SYNTH_SEG0_BETA_UV2
    g_seg0_delta_uv2 = SYNTH_SEG0_DELTA_UV2

    // Last segment with linear drift (drowsy onset)
    let mut last_alpha = SYNTH_SEG0_ALPHA_UV2 + (SYNTH_DRIFT_ALPHA_PER * last_idx)
    let     last_theta = SYNTH_SEG0_THETA_UV2 + (SYNTH_DRIFT_THETA_PER * last_idx)
    let     last_beta  = SYNTH_SEG0_BETA_UV2
    let     last_delta = SYNTH_SEG0_DELTA_UV2

    // Min alpha across all segments — nominal: smallest is seg0
    let mut min_alpha = g_seg0_alpha_uv2
    if last_alpha < min_alpha { min_alpha = last_alpha }

    if perturb_flat_alpha {
        // Channel disconnected mid-session: last segment α collapses to 0
        last_alpha = 0.0
        min_alpha  = 0.0
    }

    g_seg_last_alpha_uv2 = last_alpha
    g_seg_last_theta_uv2 = last_theta
    g_seg_last_beta_uv2  = last_beta
    g_seg_last_delta_uv2 = last_delta
    g_min_alpha_uv2      = min_alpha

    // Derived trend metrics
    g_blink_rate_per_min = SYNTH_BLINK_RATE_NOMINAL
    g_relax_index_o      = (last_alpha + g_seg0_alpha_uv2) / 2.0
    g_drowsy_signature   = safe_div(last_theta, last_alpha)
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Frozen falsifier evaluation (raw#71)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn evaluate_falsifiers() {
    // F_LR_01: actual duration >= 95% of requested
    g_f_lr_01_pass = g_duration_fraction >= F_LR_01_DURATION_FRAC

    // F_LR_02: effective fs >= 30 Hz (α Nyquist)
    g_f_lr_02_pass = g_effective_fs_hz >= F_LR_02_FS_FLOOR_HZ

    // F_LR_03: every segment α > 0 (proxy: min α across segments > floor)
    g_f_lr_03_pass = g_min_alpha_uv2 > F_LR_03_ALPHA_FLOOR
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Sentinel emit (raw#80 falsifier-bound)
//   __EEG_LONG_RESTING__ <PASS|FAIL> <duration_min> <segments>
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn emit_sentinel() {
    let mut verdict = "PASS"
    if !(g_f_lr_01_pass && g_f_lr_02_pass && g_f_lr_03_pass) {
        verdict = "FAIL"
    }
    println("__EEG_LONG_RESTING__ " + verdict + " " + to_string(g_duration_min) + " " + to_string(g_segment_count))
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Audit JSONL emit (raw#65 idempotent — single-row per ts)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn _build_audit_row(ts: string) -> string {
    let mut row = "{"
    row = row + "\"schema\":\"" + SCHEMA + "\","
    row = row + "\"ts\":\"" + ts + "\","
    row = row + "\"duration_min\":" + to_string(g_duration_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"segment_min\":" + to_string(g_segment_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"segment_count\":" + to_string(g_segment_count) + ","
    row = row + "\"total_seconds\":" + to_string(g_total_seconds) + ","
    row = row + "\"actual_duration_min\":" + to_string(g_actual_duration_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"duration_fraction\":" + to_string(g_duration_fraction) + ","
    row = row + "\"effective_fs_hz\":" + to_string(g_effective_fs_hz) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg0_alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg0_theta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_theta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg0_beta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_beta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg0_delta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_delta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg_last_alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg_last_theta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_theta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg_last_beta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_beta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"seg_last_delta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_delta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"min_alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_min_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"blink_rate_per_min\":" + to_string(g_blink_rate_per_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"relax_index_o\":" + to_string(g_relax_index_o) + ","
    row = row + "\"drowsy_signature\":" + to_string(g_drowsy_signature) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_01\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_01_pass) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_02\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_02_pass) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_03\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_03_pass)
    row = row + "}"
    return row
}

fn emit_audit(ts: string) {
    _ensure_dir(AUDIT_DIR)
    let path = AUDIT_DIR + "/" + ts + "_session.jsonl"
    let row = _build_audit_row(ts)
    let nl = chr(10)
    // raw#65 idempotent: overwrite (single-row file per ts).
    write_file(path, row + nl)
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Quality-monitoring ledger emit (paradigm=long_resting, append JSONL)
//   This is the cross-paradigm AI-side ledger that aggregates capture
//   compliance across protocols. We APPEND a row keyed by (paradigm, ts).
//   raw#65 idempotent: append to a file named by ts → re-running with same
//   ts overwrites the same single-row file (NOT the cross-session aggregate).
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn _build_ledger_row(ts: string) -> string {
    let mut verdict = "PASS"
    if !(g_f_lr_01_pass && g_f_lr_02_pass && g_f_lr_03_pass) {
        verdict = "FAIL"
    }
    let mut row = "{"
    row = row + "\"paradigm\":\"long_resting\","
    row = row + "\"schema\":\"" + SCHEMA + "\","
    row = row + "\"ts\":\"" + ts + "\","
    row = row + "\"verdict\":\"" + verdict + "\","
    row = row + "\"duration_min\":" + to_string(g_duration_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"actual_duration_min\":" + to_string(g_actual_duration_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"effective_fs_hz\":" + to_string(g_effective_fs_hz) + ","
    row = row + "\"segment_count\":" + to_string(g_segment_count) + ","
    row = row + "\"min_alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_min_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"drowsy_signature\":" + to_string(g_drowsy_signature) + ","
    row = row + "\"relax_index_o\":" + to_string(g_relax_index_o) + ","
    row = row + "\"blink_rate_per_min\":" + to_string(g_blink_rate_per_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_01\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_01_pass) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_02\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_02_pass) + ","
    row = row + "\"f_lr_03\":" + _bool_str(g_f_lr_03_pass)
    row = row + "}"
    return row
}

fn emit_ledger(ts: string) {
    _ensure_dir(LEDGER_DIR)
    let path = LEDGER_DIR + "/" + ts + "_long_resting.jsonl"
    let row = _build_ledger_row(ts)
    let nl = chr(10)
    // raw#65: per-ts file is overwritten on rerun (byte-stable for same inputs).
    write_file(path, row + nl)
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Trend metrics sidecar (JSON, alongside .npy)
//   α/θ/β/δ × first/last segment + EOG blink rate + relaxation index
//   + drowsiness signature (θ/α). Single-file overwrite (raw#65).
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn emit_trend_sidecar(output_npy: string) {
    if len(output_npy) == 0 { return }
    let path = output_npy + ".trend.json"
    let mut row = "{"
    row = row + "\"schema\":\"" + SCHEMA + "\","
    row = row + "\"npy\":\"" + output_npy + "\","
    row = row + "\"duration_min\":" + to_string(g_duration_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"segment_min\":" + to_string(g_segment_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"segment_count\":" + to_string(g_segment_count) + ","
    row = row + "\"effective_fs_hz\":" + to_string(g_effective_fs_hz) + ","
    row = row + "\"trend_first_segment\":{"
    row = row + "\"alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"theta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_theta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"beta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_beta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"delta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg0_delta_uv2)
    row = row + "},"
    row = row + "\"trend_last_segment\":{"
    row = row + "\"alpha_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_alpha_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"theta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_theta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"beta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_beta_uv2) + ","
    row = row + "\"delta_uv2\":" + to_string(g_seg_last_delta_uv2)
    row = row + "},"
    row = row + "\"eog_blink_rate_per_min\":" + to_string(g_blink_rate_per_min) + ","
    row = row + "\"relaxation_index_o\":" + to_string(g_relax_index_o) + ","
    row = row + "\"drowsy_signature_theta_alpha\":" + to_string(g_drowsy_signature) + ","
    row = row + "\"min_alpha_across_segments\":" + to_string(g_min_alpha_uv2)
    row = row + "}"
    write_file(path, row + chr(10))
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Live runner — collect.hexa subprocess delegation
//   raw#10 honest: this protocol does NOT do raw BrainFlow ingest itself;
//   it delegates to anima-eeg/collect.hexa for raw stream capture, then
//   chains sample_rate_guard + package_num_audit when --auto-quality-audit
//   is set. raw#15: no personal paths hardcoded (all CLI args).
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn print_run_plan(
    port: string,
    board: string,
    output: string,
    auto_audit: bool,
    do_ledger: bool
) {
    println("── long_duration_resting live run plan ──")
    println("schema=" + SCHEMA)
    println("port=" + port)
    println("board=" + board)
    println("output=" + output)
    println("sample_rate_hz=" + to_string(SAMPLE_RATE_HZ))
    println("channel_count=" + to_string(CHANNEL_COUNT))
    println("notch_hz=" + to_string(NOTCH_HZ))
    println("bandpass=" + to_string(BANDPASS_LO_HZ) + "-" + to_string(BANDPASS_HI_HZ) + " Hz")
    println("duration_min=" + to_string(g_duration_min))
    println("segment_min=" + to_string(g_segment_min))
    println("segment_count=" + to_string(g_segment_count))
    println("total_seconds=" + to_string(g_total_seconds))
    println("auto_quality_audit=" + _bool_str(auto_audit))
    println("ledger_emit=" + _bool_str(do_ledger))
    println("")
    println("[block design]")
    if g_segment_count == 1 {
        println("  single long capture (" + to_string(g_duration_min) + " min)")
    } else {
        println("  multi-segment: " + to_string(g_segment_count) + " × " + to_string(g_segment_min) + " min")
    }
    println("")
    println("[audio cues — minimal, every " + to_string(CUE_INTERVAL_MIN) + " min]")
    let mut t = 0
    while t < g_total_seconds {
        let cue = cue_text_at_t(t)
        println("  t=" + to_string(t) + "s  cue=\"" + cue + "\"")
        t = t + (CUE_INTERVAL_MIN * 60)
    }
    println("")
    println("[user hand-step — montage assumption]")
    println("  N1P (ch1)  -> Fp1 (forehead, 1\" above left brow)")
    println("  N2P (ch2)  -> Fp2 (forehead, 1\" above right brow)")
    println("  N7P (ch7)  -> O1  (1\" above inion, 1\" left)")
    println("  N8P (ch8)  -> O2  (1\" above inion, 1\" right)")
    println("  SRB2       -> A1 earlobe (white wire)")
    println("  BIAS       -> A2 earlobe (black wire)")
    println("")
    println("[delegate command — run in separate terminal]")
    println("  hexa run anima-eeg/collect.hexa --port " + port + " \\")
    println("      --board " + board + " --duration " + to_string(g_total_seconds) + " \\")
    println("      --output " + output)
    println("")
    if auto_audit {
        println("[auto-quality-audit chain — run after capture completes]")
        println("  hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/sample_rate_guard.hexa \\")
        println("      --input " + output + " --paradigm eeg_alpha --strict")
        println("  hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/package_num_audit.hexa \\")
        println("      --input " + output)
    }
    if do_ledger {
        println("[ledger]")
        println("  paradigm=long_resting JSONL row will land at:")
        println("  " + LEDGER_DIR + "/<TS>_long_resting.jsonl")
    }
    println("")
    println("[honest C3 reminders]")
    println("  • daily-life motion: walking / eating / bathroom = artifact")
    println("  • gel impedance drift over 30 min — re-wet at midpoint if possible")
    println("  • circadian baseline variability — log session time of day")
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Tests (selftest)
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn assert_true(cond: bool, label: string) -> bool {
    if cond { println("  PASS: " + label) } else { println("  FAIL: " + label) }
    return cond
}

fn run_tests() -> int {
    let mut pass = 0
    let mut fail = 0

    println("=== long_duration_resting selftest ===")

    // T1: schedule build — 5 min default
    println("[T1] schedule build (5 min single segment)")
    build_schedule(5, 5)
    let ok1a = assert_true(g_duration_min == 5, "duration_min == 5")
    let ok1b = assert_true(g_segment_min == 5, "segment_min == 5")
    let ok1c = assert_true(g_segment_count == 1, "segment_count == 1")
    let ok1d = assert_true(g_total_seconds == 300, "total_seconds == 300")
    if ok1a && ok1b && ok1c && ok1d { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T2: schedule build — 30 min × 5-min segments
    println("[T2] schedule build (30 min × 5-min segments)")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    let ok2a = assert_true(g_duration_min == 30, "duration_min == 30")
    let ok2b = assert_true(g_segment_min == 5, "segment_min == 5")
    let ok2c = assert_true(g_segment_count == 6, "segment_count == 6")
    let ok2d = assert_true(g_total_seconds == 1800, "total_seconds == 1800")
    if ok2a && ok2b && ok2c && ok2d { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T3: schedule build — 10 min × 5-min segments
    println("[T3] schedule build (10 min × 5-min segments)")
    build_schedule(10, 5)
    let ok3a = assert_true(g_duration_min == 10, "duration_min == 10")
    let ok3b = assert_true(g_segment_count == 2, "segment_count == 2")
    let ok3c = assert_true(g_total_seconds == 600, "total_seconds == 600")
    if ok3a && ok3b && ok3c { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T4: clamp duration into [5, 30]
    println("[T4] duration clamp [5, 30]")
    build_schedule(2, 5)
    let ok4a = assert_true(g_duration_min == 5, "below floor clamps to 5")
    build_schedule(120, 5)
    let ok4b = assert_true(g_duration_min == 30, "above ceiling clamps to 30")
    if ok4a && ok4b { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T5: idempotent schedule rebuild (raw#65)
    println("[T5] idempotent schedule rebuild")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    let segc1 = g_segment_count
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    let ok5 = assert_true(g_segment_count == segc1, "segment_count idempotent")
    if ok5 { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T6: nominal synthetic — all 3 falsifiers PASS
    println("[T6] synthetic nominal — F_LR_01/02/03 PASS")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(false, false, false)
    evaluate_falsifiers()
    let ok6a = assert_true(g_f_lr_01_pass, "F_LR_01 duration >= 95%")
    let ok6b = assert_true(g_f_lr_02_pass, "F_LR_02 effective_fs >= 30 Hz")
    let ok6c = assert_true(g_f_lr_03_pass, "F_LR_03 per-segment α > 0")
    let ok6d = assert_true(g_drowsy_signature > 0.0, "drowsy signature populated")
    if ok6a && ok6b && ok6c && ok6d { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T7: F_LR_01 falsifier — short capture (user removed cap early)
    println("[T7] F_LR_01 falsifier — short capture (80% of requested)")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(true, false, false)
    evaluate_falsifiers()
    let ok7a = assert_true(!g_f_lr_01_pass, "F_LR_01 fails (short capture)")
    let ok7b = assert_true(g_f_lr_02_pass, "F_LR_02 still passes")
    let ok7c = assert_true(g_f_lr_03_pass, "F_LR_03 still passes")
    if ok7a && ok7b && ok7c { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T8: F_LR_02 falsifier — Daisy collapse (fs ~22 Hz)
    println("[T8] F_LR_02 falsifier — effective_fs = 22 Hz (Daisy collapse)")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(false, true, false)
    evaluate_falsifiers()
    let ok8a = assert_true(g_f_lr_01_pass, "F_LR_01 still passes")
    let ok8b = assert_true(!g_f_lr_02_pass, "F_LR_02 fails (fs < 30 Hz)")
    let ok8c = assert_true(g_f_lr_03_pass, "F_LR_03 still passes")
    if ok8a && ok8b && ok8c { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T9: F_LR_03 falsifier — flat α channel mid-session
    println("[T9] F_LR_03 falsifier — α channel flat mid-session")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(false, false, true)
    evaluate_falsifiers()
    let ok9a = assert_true(g_f_lr_01_pass, "F_LR_01 still passes")
    let ok9b = assert_true(g_f_lr_02_pass, "F_LR_02 still passes")
    let ok9c = assert_true(!g_f_lr_03_pass, "F_LR_03 fails (min α == 0)")
    if ok9a && ok9b && ok9c { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T10: cue text mapping
    println("[T10] audio cue text")
    let cue0 = cue_text_at_t(0)
    let cue5 = cue_text_at_t(300)
    let ok10a = assert_true(cue0 == "측정 시작 (begin)", "t=0 cue text")
    let ok10b = assert_true(cue5 == "측정 중 t=5분 (continue)", "t=300s cue text")
    if ok10a && ok10b { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T11: audit JSONL emit (raw#65 byte-stable)
    println("[T11] audit JSONL emit deterministic")
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(false, false, false)
    evaluate_falsifiers()
    let ts = "selftest_synth"
    emit_audit(ts)
    let body1 = read_file(AUDIT_DIR + "/" + ts + "_session.jsonl")
    emit_audit(ts)
    let body2 = read_file(AUDIT_DIR + "/" + ts + "_session.jsonl")
    let ok11a = assert_true(body1 == body2, "audit row byte-stable")
    let ok11b = assert_true(len(body1) > 0, "audit row non-empty")
    if ok11a && ok11b { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    // T12: ledger JSONL emit (raw#65 byte-stable)
    println("[T12] ledger JSONL emit deterministic")
    emit_ledger(ts)
    let lbody1 = read_file(LEDGER_DIR + "/" + ts + "_long_resting.jsonl")
    emit_ledger(ts)
    let lbody2 = read_file(LEDGER_DIR + "/" + ts + "_long_resting.jsonl")
    let ok12a = assert_true(lbody1 == lbody2, "ledger row byte-stable")
    let ok12b = assert_true(len(lbody1) > 0, "ledger row non-empty")
    if ok12a && ok12b { pass = pass + 1 } else { fail = fail + 1 }

    println("")
    println("Results: " + to_string(pass) + " PASS / " + to_string(fail) + " FAIL out of " + to_string(pass + fail))
    return fail
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CLI entry
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

fn _print_usage() {
    println("usage:")
    println("  hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --selftest")
    println("  hexa run anima-eeg/protocols/long_duration_resting.hexa --run \\")
    println("      --port <serial> --board cyton_daisy --duration <minutes> \\")
    println("      [--segment-minutes <n>] [--auto-quality-audit] [--ledger] \\")
    println("      [--output <npy>]")
}

fn _arg_value(av: list, key: string, dflt: string) -> string {
    let mut i = 1
    while i < len(av) {
        if av[i] == key && i + 1 < len(av) {
            return av[i + 1]
        }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return dflt
}

fn _arg_int(av: list, key: string, dflt: int) -> int {
    let s = _arg_value(av, key, "")
    if len(s) == 0 { return dflt }
    return to_int(s)
}

fn _arg_flag(av: list, key: string) -> bool {
    let mut i = 1
    while i < len(av) {
        if av[i] == key { return true }
        i = i + 1
    }
    return false
}

fn main() {
    let av = argv()
    let mut selftest = false
    let mut run = false
    let mut i = 1
    while i < len(av) {
        if av[i] == "--selftest" { selftest = true }
        if av[i] == "--run"      { run = true }
        if av[i] == "--help"     { _print_usage(); exit(0) }
        i = i + 1
    }

    if run {
        let port       = _arg_value(av, "--port",   "")
        let board      = _arg_value(av, "--board",  "cyton_daisy")
        let output     = _arg_value(av, "--output", "")
        let dur_min    = _arg_int(av,   "--duration",         DEFAULT_DURATION_MIN)
        let seg_min    = _arg_int(av,   "--segment-minutes",  DEFAULT_SEGMENT_MIN)
        let auto_audit = _arg_flag(av,  "--auto-quality-audit")
        let do_ledger  = _arg_flag(av,  "--ledger")

        if len(port) == 0 {
            eprintln("ABORT: --run requires --port (raw#15 no personal paths)")
            _print_usage()
            exit(2)
        }

        build_schedule(dur_min, seg_min)
        print_run_plan(port, board, output, auto_audit, do_ledger)

        // raw#10 honest: this cycle prints plan + delegated commands;
        // the actual collect.hexa subprocess + sample_rate_guard +
        // package_num_audit + ledger emit are user hand-steps after the
        // capture .npy lands. The plan is logged; ledger row is emitted
        // here as a placeholder (verdict reflects schedule build only —
        // post-capture analysis must rerun emit_ledger with real values).
        if do_ledger {
            // Placeholder pre-capture ledger emit: marks intent.
            // verdict will be recomputed post-capture by analysis pass.
            g_effective_fs_hz       = 0.0
            g_actual_duration_min   = 0.0
            g_duration_fraction     = 0.0
            g_min_alpha_uv2         = 0.0
            evaluate_falsifiers()
            emit_ledger("plan_" + to_string(dur_min) + "min")
        }
        exit(0)
    }

    if !selftest {
        _print_usage()
        exit(2)
    }

    println("── long_duration_resting selftest ──")
    println("schema=" + SCHEMA)
    println("raw10_honest=synthetic_trend_no_real_brainflow_terminal_only")
    println("raw82_darwin=clock_gettime_monotonic_via_collect_hexa")
    println("source=anima-eeg/protocols/alpha_eyes_closed.hexa_v1_extension")
    println("")

    // Demonstration (synthetic 30 min × 5 min × 6 segments)
    build_schedule(30, 5)
    analyze_synthetic_trend(false, false, false)
    evaluate_falsifiers()

    println("[demo nominal session — 30 min × 6 segments]")
    println("duration_min="          + to_string(g_duration_min))
    println("segment_min="           + to_string(g_segment_min))
    println("segment_count="         + to_string(g_segment_count))
    println("total_seconds="         + to_string(g_total_seconds))
    println("actual_duration_min="   + to_string(g_actual_duration_min))
    println("duration_fraction="     + to_string(g_duration_fraction))
    println("effective_fs_hz="       + to_string(g_effective_fs_hz))
    println("seg0_alpha_uv2="        + to_string(g_seg0_alpha_uv2))
    println("seg_last_alpha_uv2="    + to_string(g_seg_last_alpha_uv2))
    println("seg0_theta_uv2="        + to_string(g_seg0_theta_uv2))
    println("seg_last_theta_uv2="    + to_string(g_seg_last_theta_uv2))
    println("min_alpha_uv2="         + to_string(g_min_alpha_uv2))
    println("blink_rate_per_min="    + to_string(g_blink_rate_per_min))
    println("relax_index_o="         + to_string(g_relax_index_o))
    println("drowsy_signature="      + to_string(g_drowsy_signature))
    println("f_lr_01="               + _bool_str(g_f_lr_01_pass))
    println("f_lr_02="               + _bool_str(g_f_lr_02_pass))
    println("f_lr_03="               + _bool_str(g_f_lr_03_pass))
    println("")

    emit_sentinel()
    emit_audit("selftest_synth")
    emit_ledger("selftest_synth")

    let fails = run_tests()
    if fails != 0 {
        println("selftest=fail")
        eprintln("selftest FAILED: " + to_string(fails) + " test(s) failed")
        exit(1)
    }
    println("selftest=ok")
    println("DONE")
}

// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HONEST C3 CAVEATS  (raw#10) — full text
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// (1) Daily-life motion artifact (walking / eating / bathroom).
//     The user runs this with the cap on during normal activity. Walking
//     introduces step-rate (~2 Hz) movement artifact; chewing introduces
//     EMG bleed into the 20-50 Hz band; bathroom transitions cause cable
//     tug. The protocol does NOT excise these epochs — sidecar trend
//     metrics are computed across the full segment and will be biased by
//     motion-laden intervals. Mitigation: log activity-of-interval; use
//     analyze.hexa epoch-level rejection in a follow-up cycle. (raw#10 C3.)
//
// (2) Cap gel impedance drift over 30 minutes.
//     Saline / gel electrodes dry out gradually; impedance can rise from
//     ~5 kΩ (start) to >50 kΩ (30 min) on uncovered sites. This shifts
//     the noise floor and reduces α/β SNR over time. F_LR_03 catches
//     full disconnect (min α == 0) but does NOT catch graded SNR loss.
//     Mitigation: re-wet at midpoint when feasible; flag last-segment
//     alpha < 50% of first-segment alpha as drift candidate (sidecar
//     annotation, not falsifier). (raw#10 C3.)
//
// (3) Circadian-state baseline variability.
//     α power, θ/α ratio, and blink rate vary by time-of-day, sleep
//     debt, and meal state (postprandial drowsiness). A single 30-min
//     session is NOT a stable baseline — cross-session aggregation in
//     state/quality_monitoring_ledger/ is required to separate within-
//     session trend (drowsiness onset) from across-session circadian
//     drift. The ledger paradigm=long_resting row carries duration_min,
//     drowsy_signature, and relax_index_o so a follow-up cycle can do
//     time-of-day / circadian regression. (raw#10 C3.)
